Hi Justus

If you are trying to match a single treatment to multiple controls, you
might look at "synthetic control" methods, by Abadie and colleagues maybe?

Abadie, Alberto, and Javier Gardeazabal, 2003, “The Economic Costs of
Conflict: A Case Study of the Basque Country,” American Economic Review,
http://www.jstor.org/stable/3132164

Abadie, Alberto, Alexis Diamond, and Jens Hainmueller, 2008, “Synthetic
Control Methods for
Comparative Case Studies: Estimating the Effect of California’s Tobacco
Control Program,” Journal of the American Statistical Association,
http://dx.doi.org/10.1198/jasa.2009.ap08746

Matthieu

